# Release tarballs are NOT committed. SHA256SUMS + SHA256SUMS.asc are, and
# they are signed by the builder threshold — that is the trust anchor, and it
# makes any later download of the tarball verifiable. Committing ~86MB of
# already-compressed bytes per release per arch adds no integrity, only
# permanent history. See 'Why the tarball is not committed' in CLAUDE.md.
upstream/*.tar.gz

provenance.json
contents-manifest.json
sbom.spdx.json
# Per-platform predicates for a multi-arch release (make verify-published).
predicates/
keys/trusted-fingerprints.txt.candidate

# Private signing keys. cosign.pub is committed on purpose — consumers need it —
# but the private half must never be. `make check-pins` fails if a private key
# ever becomes tracked, because .gitignore alone does not protect against
# `git add -f` or a key that was committed before a rule existed.
cosign.key
*.key
!keys/*.asc
